    <statement><p>Consider the function <m>f(x,y,z) = xy + yz^2 + xz^3</m>.</p>
<p>Find the gradient of <m>f</m>:</p>
<p><m>\langle</m><fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/>, <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/>, <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/><m>\rangle</m></p>
<p>Find the gradient of <m>f</m> at
the point (-2, 3, -5).</p>
<p><m>\langle</m><fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0004"/>, <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0005"/>, <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0006"/><m>\rangle</m></p>
<p>Find the rate of change of the function <m>f</m> at the point (-2, 3,-5)  in the direction 
<m>\mathbf u = \langle -2/\sqrt{9}, -1/\sqrt{9}, 2/\sqrt{9} \rangle</m>.</p>
<p><fillin characters="60" name="AnSwEr0007"/></p>
</statement>
